# Scratch space for DAST runs. Contains the generated DAST-safe OpenAPI document
# and the ZAP reports, both of which are build outputs, and the reports can
# contain request and response bodies from a scan against staging. This
# repository is public, so nothing from here is ever committed.
zap/work/

# Generated by security/bola/route-matrix.mjs from the OpenAPI spec. Derived,
# not authored: committing it would create a second source of truth that can
# disagree with the spec, which is the exact failure the enumerator exists to
# prevent.
bola/route-matrix.json

# The material that is deliberately NOT published: the accepted-risk register
# and every dated audit and DAST findings report. Each one is defensible on its
# own; read together they are an inventory of which control is weak, until when,
# and what compensates for it, in a repository that also publishes the hostnames
# those controls protect. See README.md section "What is not in this directory".
#
# This is a working directory, not the store of record. The store of record is a
# separate PRIVATE repository; this path exists so a checkout of it can sit here
# and the tooling can find it without an environment variable. Nothing under it
# is ever committed here.
private/
